 "note": "DERIVE_FROM_BEHAVIOR v1: 16 exported pure functions (typed number / string / boolean params and result) from 15 permissive repos outside lm-corpus. Examples are the upstream function run on a fixed input grid (every 3rd row, at most 14, as the starting training slice), extended only by following PeaceAI's own derive_under_specified refusals the way an issue author would (each added row and the gate that asked for it is in addedForGates; Auditor #491 B1); held out: the rest of the grid plus every probe point (neighbour and far probes) not in the training rows; the prose is the function's leading doc comment only (empty for 6), never its body. PeaceAI derives the recorded expression from the training examples alone (the prose is recorded for review and never given to the engine); it is right on every held-out row, and each recorded expression was reviewed equal to the upstream body on its whole typed domain (template literal = concatenation; the ternary and comparisons as written). The evidence test re-derives each expression from the recorded examples and checks the pinned module text contains the upstream function; no third-party code is run by the test.",
 "examples": [
